ny environments  could be challenging for older  developers as time goes on  senior developers start to notice they  are on the older side of the team  and find themselves in a pool of younger  programmers  many can't connect with the younger  teammates because of the generation gap  and some other factors they might feel  lonely in the workplace  fifth the startup culture favors younger  developers  startup founders try to go fast and  break things  every entrepreneur's dream is to change  the world in some positive way  an idea is a fragile thing execution is  everything  but before the execution entrepreneurs  need some tech products  they can't afford to wait a long time  for a product to be built  because when an idea fails entrepreneurs  have to learn from the mistakes and  pivot into another direction  all these experiments require fast  development  so for cheap and fast product  development entrepreneurs  always look for younger software  engineers  older developers face concerns about the  stability of the roles they're in  which can lead to heightened stress this  can be avoided by taking early  preparation  the most important factor in staying  employed as a senior software developer  is to stay relevant  companies don't hire young programmers  because they're young  they hire them because their skills are  relevant  older programmers will have no problems  staying employed or finding new  engineering jobs if they decide to keep  their skills relevant  at all times keep up with programming  methodologies  and learn new technologies in other  words software developers who want to  stay in this profession for a long time  need to follow the unmind if you have a  young mind  whatever age you are will matter less  if you found this video useful i would  appreciate it if you smash the like  button  also make sure to subscribe to the  coding tech channel and click on the  notification bell  enjoy the rest of your day
 

